# prettier-plugin-astro cannot PARSE a <script> nested inside a template
# expression, and this file renders its flip-card script as `{flip && (<script>
# ... </script>)}` so a page that does not opt in ships no JS. Prettier exits 2
# on it (a hard parse error, not a formatting difference), which took the whole
# `pnpm run format` run down with it and is why source formatting could never be
# gated. Verified the trigger is the nesting, not the TypeScript generics in the
# script: the same generics in a top-level <script> format fine, and removing
# them here does not help. The fix that removes this exemption is to move the
# script into its own small component with a top-level <script> and render that
# conditionally; doing it here would mean reshaping a shared visual primitive.
apps/web/src/components/ui/LogoGrid.astro
